{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1486821-homebrew-path-examples","id":1486821,"title":"Homebrew Path Examples?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-17T18:50:00-07:00","id":1486821,"title":"Homebrew Path Examples?","content":"I'm helping my players create characters for our upcoming Aberrant game. We are new to the Trinity Continuum games and Storypath system. Has anyone created any homebrew Paths they are willing to share? I'm hoping to expand my player's options. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T19:36:29-07:00","id":1486830,"title":"","content":"Sure, though I'll spare you the ones I've written that are too specific to my game world.<br /> <br /> <u>Origin Paths</u><br /> Former Experimental Subject<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Culture, Humanities, Science, Technology<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Ambidextrous, Artifact, Covert, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Hardy, Striking<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Stamina, Culture, Technology<br /> (must take 2 dots in Covert at first dot in path)<br /> <br /> International Traveler<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics, Culture, Humanities, Survival<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Alternate Identity, Dual Citizenship, Fame, Free Running, Safe House, Wealth<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Presence, Culture, Humanities<br /> <br /> <u>Role Paths</u><br /> <br /> Treasure Hunter<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Culture, Enigmas, Humanities, Larceny<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Dual Citizenship, Artifact, Weak Spots, Speed Reading, Adrenaline Spike, Library, Direction Sense, Always Prepared<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Cunning, Enigmas, Larceny<br /> <br /> Research Specialist<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Enigmas, Humanities, Science, Technology<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Library, Patron, Weak Spots, Photographic Memory, Speed Reading, Artistic Talent, Keen Sense<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Intellect, Enigmas, Humanities<br /> <br /> <u>Society Paths</u><br /> <br /> US Army Ranger<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Aim, Athletics, Close Combat, Survival<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Always Prepared, Hardy, Iron Will, Small Unit Tactics, Breath Control, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Tough Cookie<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Aim, Close Combat, Survival<br /> <br /> Freelance Reporter<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Culture, Humanities, Integrity, Persuasion<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Dual Citizenship, Photographic Memory, Library, Speed Reading, Skilled Liar, Safe House, Keen Sense, Weak Spots, Fame<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Empathy, Humanities, Persuasion<br /> <br /> Tech Industry Insider<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Culture, Integrity, Persuasion, Technology<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Fame, Lightning Calculator, Patron, Skilled Liar, Wealth<br /> <b>Gifts: </b>Culture, Persuasion, Technology<br /> <br /> Hacker Collective<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Enigmas, Integrity, Persuasion, Technology<br /> <b>Edges: </b>Forgery (2), Darkest Web (2), Conspirators (3), Bolthole (3), Safehouse, Wealth (5)<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Enigmas, Persuasion, Technology<br /> <br /> Professional Thief<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics, Close Combat, Integrity, Larceny<br /> <b>Edges: </b>Always Prepared, Polyglot, Criminal Contact (2), Fame<br /> <b>Gifts: </b>Athletics, Integrity, Larceny<br /> <br /> They're really easy to do as you need them. I hope these give you some ideas. They should all be legal, but I don't promise there aren't errors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T00:07:01-07:00","id":1486849,"title":"","content":"I run for now <b>Scion </b>2E - and there is nice Community Content with that, about Paths for Scion. Half of them are easily to use in Trinity also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/358684/Divine-Identities\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ine-Identities</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-18-2022, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T17:48:29-07:00","id":1486928,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much Slagheap and Wyrdhamster! these are great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T17:49:27-07:00","id":1487522,"title":"","content":"If you've not seen it, there is a downloadable PDF file from Onyx Path called <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/347352/Trinity-Continuum-New-Lives\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum: New Lives</a>, which includes several new Origin and Role paths. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T19:40:14-07:00","id":1487676,"title":"","content":"Thank you No One of Consequence! This PDF is very helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T11:11:20-07:00","id":1493587,"title":"","content":"Because I had some time on my hands, a few Origin paths. Some of these are mild variations of the existing ones, but others are new. <br /> <br /> <b>Rural (Origin) </b><br /> You grew up far from the urban world, be it a family farm, ranch lands, or some other isolated homestead. Neighbors were few and far between, but your family was likely close knit. You know how to take care of yourself and your things. <br /> <i>Connections</i>: Members of your extended family, the County sheriff, Animal veterinarians, Local militia, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Aim, Athletics, Integrity, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Always Prepared, Animal Ken, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Hardy, Keen Sense, Sniper, Swift, Tough Cookie<br /> <br /> <b>Small Town (Origin)</b><br /> You come from a small town or village, a place where everyone knows each other (for better or worse), going back a long ways. <br /> <i>Connections</i>: Town government, Local librarian, Former neighbors, Town newspaper, Family doctor<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Empathy, Humanities, Persuasion, Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Artistic Talent, Big Hearted, Iron Will, Ms. Fix-It, Skilled Liar, Swift, Tough Cookie, Weak Spots<br /> <br /> <b>Working Class (Origin)</b><br /> From a proud line of factory workers, miners, or other skilled labor, you grew up respecting hard work and people who do it. Both home and co-workers formed the backbone of your life. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Family members, Labor and trade unions, Local store owners, Labor activist lawyers<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Command, Culture, Empathy, Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Artistic Talent, Big Hearted, Iron Will, Ms. Fix-It, Patron, Tough Cookie, Weak Spots<br /> <br /> <b>Child of the Streets (Origin)</b><br /> Be it as a runaway, a product of neglectful parents, or some other reason, you made your way through the meaner corners of the city while growing up. What you might lack in formal education, you make up for with street smarts and tenacity. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Homeless shelter, Street gang, Former mentor, Police officer, Medical clinic<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics, Enigmas, Larceny, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Alternate Identity, Danger Sense, Free Running, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Skilled Liar, Small Unit Tactics, Tough Cookie<br /> <br /> <b>Suburbia (Origin)</b><br /> While not necessarily the white picket fences and green lawns of stereotypes, you grew up in a fairly descent neighborhood with a financially stable family. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Life-long best friend, Former teacher, Family member, Former classmates with interesting jobs<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Empathy, Humanities, Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Artistic Talent, Big Hearted, Library, Patron, Wealth<br /> <br /> <b>Life of Privilege (Origin)</b><br /> You were born among the elite and raised that way, with the best schools and best toys. Outside of the US, this can easily include a nation's nobility or other heirs to power. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Family business interests, School alumni, Political groups with ties to your family, Family lawyer or financial manager, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Command, Culture, Integrity, Persuasion<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Fame, Patron, Skilled Liar, Striking, Wealth<br /> <br /> <br /> More later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T12:05:30-07:00","id":1493591,"title":"","content":"And more.<br /> <br /> <b>Latch Key Kid (Origin)</b><br /> Because of either a single parent or both parents working, you mainly learned to raise yourself (and perhaps your siblings) from a young age. While still having many of the benefits of a stable home, you were able to take advantage of your freedom to live an interesting life. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Landlord, Local busybody, Life-long Best friend, Siblings, Neighbor who kept an eye on you, Local oddball<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Integrity, Larceny, Persuasion, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Always Prepared, Animal Ken, Big Hearted, Iron Will, Hardy, Ms. Fix It, Skilled Liar, any one Sense edge<br /> <br /> <b>Underdog (Origin)</b><br /> You were born behind the eight ball, so to speak. Be it chronic illness, being the runt of the litter, or just constant bad luck, you always had to work overtime to get what you wanted and be successful. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Social worker, Local priest, Former trainer or teacher<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics OR Close Combat, Culture, Empathy, Integrity<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Big Hearted, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Iron Will, Patron, Swift, Weak Spots, Free Running OR Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <b>Prodigy (Origin)</b><br /> A born genius in your field, your special talents were encouraged and cultivated from a young age.<br /> <i>Connections: </i>Prominent think tank or lab, Former teacher, Other luminaries in your chosen field<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Enigmas, Medicine, Science, Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Covert OR Fame, Library, Lightning Calculator, Patron, Photographic Memory, Speed Reading<br /> <br /> <b>Bookworm (Origin)</b><br /> You grew up with a love of books and the worlds they opened up to you. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Famous author, Professional researcher, Rare book collector<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Enigmas, Humanities, Science<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Artistic Talent, Iron Will, Library, Lightning Calculator, Photographic Memory, Speed Reading<br /> <br /> <b>Jock (Origin)</b><br /> Sports and athletics have always been your thing.<br /> <i>Connections: </i>Former teammates, Sports doctor, Former coach<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics (required), Command, Culture, Medicine<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Big Hearted, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Iron Will, Small Unit Tactics, Swift, Tough Cookie, Free Running OR Martial Arts<br /> <br /> More later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T14:08:03-07:00","id":1493644,"title":"","content":"Once more into the breach.<br /> <br /> <b>Nomadic (Origin)</b><br /> You grew up moving from place to place, perhaps as a military brat or as a member of a traditional nomadic culture. Either way, you've been a lot of different places and no how to adjust to new circumstances. <br /> <i>Connections:</i> Extended family members, Fellow travelers, Smugglers, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Larceny, Pilot, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Covert, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Iron Will, Patron, Skilled Liar, Tough Cookie, any one Sense edge<br /> <br /> <b>Primitive (Origin)</b><br /> You come from a pre-industrial culture apart from much of the modern world. This includes certain religious and other sects who shun modern technology. <br /> <i>Connections:</i> Fellow tribe members, Government agencies dealing with your people, Anthropologist <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Aim, Integrity, Medicine, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Animal Ken, Breath Control, Covert, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Hardy, Keen Sense, Small Unit Tactics, Swift<br /> <br /> <b>War Torn (Origin)</b><br /> You grew up in a war zone or in a region very recently impacted by conflict, and learned at an early age how to survive and potentially fight back.<br /> <i>Connections: </i>Refugees, Non-Government Agencies, Soldiers, Black Market<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Aim, Close Combat, Medicine, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Always Prepared, Covert, Danger Sense, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Safe House, Small Unit Tactics OR Cool Under Fire, any one Style edge<br /> <br /> <b>Monastery (Origin)</b><br /> Raised among a religious cloister. While this is mainly meant for various Eastern traditions, it can just as easily cover certain Western orders as well. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Monastery leader, Fellow monks/nuns, Religious scholars<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics, Close Combat, Enigmas, Integrity<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Breath Control, Covert, Iron Will, Keen Sense, any one Martial Arts edge, Swift, Tough Cookie, Weak Spots<br /> <br /> <b>Ward (Origin)</b><br /> You were brought up by someone other than your family, be it a state agency, wealthy billionaire, or other surrogate. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Former guardian, Social worker, Lawyer, Fellow wards<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics, Empathy, Integrity, Larceny<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Alternate Identity, Danger Sense, Patron, Safe House, Skilled Liar, Wealth, Weak Spots<br /> <br /> <b>Cult (Origin)</b><br /> You were raised (indoctrinated) by a group at odds with normal society, be it for religious or political reasons, and trained to carry out their doctrine and goals. You may or may not still be a member of said group, depending on circumstances. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Cult leader, Former cult members, Deprogrammer, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Aim, Integrity, Persuasion, Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Alternate Identity, Covert, Hardy OR Iron Will, Skilled Liar, Small Unit Tactics, any one Style edge<br /> <br /> <b>Alien (Origin)</b><br /> You are ... not of this world. Possibly from another world, another time, or another reality, or perhaps just so odd that you have never fit in with any normal society. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Fringe scientist, Conspiracy theorist, Rogue government agent<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Empathy, Enigmas, Integrity, Science OR Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Alternate Identity, Covert, Keen Sense, Striking, Artifact, Superior Trait<br /> <br /> And that's it for Origins. Next is Roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T14:53:21-07:00","id":1493647,"title":"","content":"Some alternate and/or new Role paths. <br /> <br /> <b>Ace (Role)</b><br /> Be it land, sea, or air, you are a master pilot at one with your chosen vehicle (or perhaps any vehicle).<br /> <i>Connections: </i>Fellow pilots, Former clients, Mechanic, Airport/Garage/Pier owner, Vehicle manufacturer <br /> <i>Skills</i>: Aim, Command, Pilot (required), Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Ambidextrous, Always Prepared, Cool Under Fire, Direction Sense, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Lightning Calculator, Ms. Fix It, Patron<br /> <br /> <b>Survivalist (Role)</b><br /> You can survive and even thrive in the harshest of conditions with little or no support. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Fellow outdoorsmen, Cryptozoologist, Conspiracy theorist, Native guide, Gear manufacturer<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Medicine, Survival, any two of Aim, Athletics OR Close Combat<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Always Prepared, Animal Ken, Covert, Direction Sense, Hardy, Iron Will, Keen Sense, Swift<br /> <br /> <b>Everyperson (Role)</b><br /> Just your average, everyday normal person. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Neighbors, Coworkers, Family members, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Empathy, Integrity, Humanities OR Technology<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Always Prepared, Animal Ken, Big Hearted, Covert, Cool Under Fire, Direction Sense, Swift, Weak Points, any 3 point edge<br /> <br /> <b>Occultist (Role)</b><br /> You delve into the mysteries of magic, the paranormal, and other areas beyond everyday life.<br /> <i>Connections: </i>Fellow seekers, Parapsychology group, Anthropologist, Professional psychic/shaman<br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Enigmas, Integrity, Command OR Persuasion <br /> <i>Edges: </i>Alternate Identity, Breath Control, Covert OR Fame, Danger Sense, Iron Will, Library, Safe House, <br /> <br /> <b>Traveler (Role)</b><br /> An old hand at international travel, you've been nearly everywhere and can easily find your footing in any new location. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Pilot, Ship captain, Jet Setters, International journalists, Local guide, Diplomat, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Culture, Empathy, Persuasion, Pilot OR Survival<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Alternate Identity, Always Prepared, Animal Ken, Direction Sense, Hardy, Safe House, Wealth<br /> <br /> <b>Pillar (Role)</b><br /> Be it as assistant, sidekick, or any other role, you are the rock your group can always rely on. <br /> <i>Connections: </i>Household or other support staff, Lawyer, Doctor, Martial arts instructor, Lifelong Friend, <br /> <i>Skills: </i>Athletics, Empathy, Integrity, any ONE of Close Combat, Medicine, OR Pilot<br /> <i>Edges: </i>Adrenaline Spike, Always Prepared, Danger Sense, Big Hearted, Patron, Martial Arts, Safe House, Swift, any ONE of Cool Under Fire, Ms Fix It, OR Skilled Liar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}